# Copied to .gitignore in the published repository by scripts/publish.sh.
#
# Named without the leading dot on purpose: a real .gitignore in publish/ would apply to this directory of the source repository rather than to the published one.
#
# Almost nothing is ignored there --- the whole point of that repository is that the built site is committed --- so this covers only what a reader creates locally after cloning.
#
# Note what is NOT here: a student's own working files. This course asks them to commit their work, and a .gitignore that quietly swallowed it would be teaching the opposite of Unit 1.

# Jupyter leftovers from opening the activity notebooks.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Whatever environment a student builds for themselves in Unit 4. None of these are created by anything shipped here; they are here because a student who follows the unit will make one.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
renv/

.DS_Store
